reason:
The code in clip-test.ipynb Cell 3 (RetinopathyDataset.__init__) uses an explicit Python-level loop over df.groupby('level') that could be replaced with vectorized pandas operations. Specifically, the for loop:
```python
for k,v in df.groupby('level'):
    if len(v) < 1000:
        data[k] = v
    else:
        data[k] = v.iloc[:len(v),:]
```
Both branches of the if/else do the identical thing (`v.iloc[:len(v),:]` equals `v`), making the entire loop redundant. The data could simply be `self.data = df` without any iteration. Even if truncation was intended, it could be done with `df.groupby('level').head(1000)`. The list comprehension `[data[i] for i in range(5)]` could also be replaced with `list(data.values())`.
